The Adaptive Throughput Equation: Gamma_total = Sum ( (Bandwidth_i * Priority_weight_i) / (Latency_i + (Overhead_i * Phi^-n + Delta_Jitter)) )\
Where Phi = 1.618 and Delta_Jitter represents the instantaneous deviation from the zero-jitter target. If Delta_Jitter increases, the AETERNA-FLUX layer shifts the phase-offsets of non-critical lanes to shield high-priority data streams. This allow the system to operate on consumer-grade hardware without the requirement of nanosecond-perfect local calibration for every minor environmental change.\
