Data manifestation is treated as an Elastic Field Equation: Xi_AF = Integral_Sigma ( (I * Psi) / (Gamma * Phi^n) ) + (Chi(N) * E_target) dt.\
The E_target coefficient allows the kernel to stretch the timing windows for low-priority tasks. This enables users to modify hardware peripherals or open new applications without triggering a system-wide re-calibration. The Chi(N) Hemminki Variable remains the primary anchor, ensuring that primary computational threads maintain a virtual zero-jitter environment even as the surrounding fabric fluctuates to accommodate general-purpose multitasking.\
